From 88fbbdfdf3bb244ac93d3b9596b411a7ad6edcb3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chandan <chandan@medpath-lab.dev>
Date: Sat, 11 Jul 2026 13:59:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Patient Registration: split into focused cards, fix dark-mode
 toast bug, color-role consistency
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Senior review pass on top of the previously-applied progress-summary
patch. Decisions made and applied directly:

1. Split Personal Details into 4 cards (Priority 4 / 21, High)
   Identity, Contact and Address are now standalone lis-cards
   instead of field-groups stacked inside one ever-taller container.
   A step-header card holds the title, Personal/Clinical toggle,
   progress bar and duplicate-patient banner. Cards get a real 16px
   gap instead of the old glued single-card + flush-footer layout;
   the action bar is now a standalone, fully-rounded bar to match.
   Clinical Information (Step 2) already lived in its own card/step
   and needed no structural change.

2. Consistent section header treatment (Priority 3 / 18)
   All card headers on this screen — including Clinical Information
   — now share the same 28px icon badge + font-weight 600 title
   already used for the Visit Details / Preparation / Medication
   groups, instead of a plain small glyph.

3. Fixed a real dark-mode bug in the '\''saved'\'' toast
   .step-saved-toast used --lis-primary-deep as a solid background
   with white text. --lis-primary-deep is a foreground-text token
   that intentionally flips per theme (near-black in light mode,
   near-white in dark mode, confirmed across all 4 palettes) — using
   it as a solid fill made the toast nearly invisible in dark mode.
   Swapped to --lis-primary, which stays a consistent brand teal in
   both themes and matches how .lis-btn--primary already pairs white
   text with --lis-primary app-wide.

4. Color-role consistency for primary vs primary-deep
   Established one rule for this screen: --lis-primary for
   structural/branding elements (icons, borders, fills, buttons),
   --lis-primary-deep for small-text foreground content, since it's
   specifically tuned per theme for text-level contrast.
     - .ok-msg (mobile-valid message): primary -> primary-deep
     - .reg-progress__label--done: primary -> primary-deep
   (.gender-card--active and the success/PID block already followed
   this rule correctly and were left unchanged.)

Verified with npx ng build --configuration development — clean build.
